# confirm — a preview fails exactly where --confirm would (INVARIANTS.md H-2),
# asked as the TWO questions the rule actually contains:
#
#   [target]  does the identifier the command writes to resolve, before a plan?
#   [value]   is everything else the caller supplied judged, before a plan?
#
# The surface is the live cobra tree, walked by TestConfirmSurfaceIsClosed, two
# sites per --confirm command. It carried ONE site per command until 2026-07-31,
# and that is how two commands shipped as `proven` while accepting values Home
# Assistant refuses: `svc call` was proven by a test that resolves the SERVICE
# while `--data '{"target":{…}}'` reached HA unexamined and answered 400, and
# `ent rename`'s one malformed-id case was `nodomain` while five other shapes HA
# refuses previewed as "would rename … references: 2" at exit 0. Neither row was
# false. Both answered one of two questions under a key that asked both.
#
# `proven` is claimed only where a test asserts the *refusal* — an unresolvable
# target, or a value the confirmed run cannot use, ending the command. A test
# that only asserts the preview does not write proves the other half of H-2.
#
# The ceiling is the number of sites known to be unproven. It may fall without
# ceremony and may only rise by editing this line on purpose.
#ceiling 30

# --- targets: a named test asserts the preview refuses an unresolvable one ----
hactl auto delete [target] = proven: TestAutoDeleteDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl script delete [target] = proven: TestScriptDeleteDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl tpl delete [target] = proven: TestTplDeleteDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl helper delete [target] = proven: TestHelperDeleteDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl area delete [target] = proven: TestRegistryDeleteDryRunResolvesTarget
hactl floor delete [target] = proven: TestRegistryDeleteDryRunResolvesTarget
hactl label delete [target] = proven: TestRegistryDeleteDryRunResolvesTarget
hactl config delete [target] = proven: TestConfigDeleteDryRunRefusesUnknownEntry
hactl dash delete [target] = proven: TestDashDeleteAgreesOnUnknownDashboard
hactl script apply [target] = proven: TestE2EDryRunRejectsFabricatedTargetCLI
hactl script run [target] = proven: TestRunScriptRun_NotFound
hactl auto apply [target] = proven: TestAutoApplyDryRunRefusesUnresolvableTarget
hactl svc call [target] = proven: TestSvcCallDryRunRefusesAServiceHADoesNotHave
hactl device set-area [target] = proven: TestDeviceSetAreaDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl device set-label [target] = proven: TestDeviceSetLabelDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl ent rename [target] = proven: TestEntRenameDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl helper create [target] = proven: TestHelperCreatePreviewAgreesWithConfirmOnEveryLayout

# --- values: a named test asserts the preview refuses an unusable one ---------
hactl script create [value] = proven: TestCreateDryRunRejectsUnusableInput
hactl helper create [value] = proven: TestCreateDryRunRejectsUnusableInput
hactl auto create [value] = proven: TestAutoCreate_MalformedYAMLRefused_DryRun
hactl area create [value] = proven: TestRegistryCreateRefusesABlankName
hactl floor create [value] = proven: TestRegistryCreateRefusesABlankName
hactl label create [value] = proven: TestRegistryCreateRefusesABlankName
hactl dash create [value] = proven: TestRunDashCreate_DryRunResolvesItsInput
hactl svc call [value] = proven: TestUnknownFieldsRefusesWhatHomeAssistantRefuses
hactl ent rename [value] = proven: TestEntRenameDryRunRefusesUnresolvable
hactl auto apply [value] = proven: TestWriter_ApplyWritesTheBytesTheDiffShowed

# The three registry creates were exempt from this surface entirely until
# 2026-07-30, on the reading that "the argument names something that does not
# exist yet, so there is no target to resolve". True of the [target] half, and
# beside the point: H-2's other half judges the VALUE, and `area create ""
# --confirm` then created a real area with a blank area_id on a production
# instance and took down every `area` command until a raw WebSocket call removed
# it. Splitting the surface is that lesson made structural — an exemption argued
# from one half of a rule is how the other half goes unenforced.

# --- exempt: the question does not arise here --------------------------------
hactl companion wireguard config [target] = exempt: operates on the add-on the companion runs in and takes no caller-supplied identifier
hactl companion wireguard up [target] = exempt: operates on the add-on the companion runs in and takes no caller-supplied identifier
hactl companion wireguard down [target] = exempt: operates on the add-on the companion runs in and takes no caller-supplied identifier
hactl companion wireguard up [value] = exempt: brings the tunnel the add-on already holds up; there is no caller-supplied value to judge
hactl companion wireguard down [value] = exempt: takes the tunnel the add-on already holds down; there is no caller-supplied value to judge
hactl script create [target] = exempt: a create names nothing yet — the id is derived from the file, whose refusal is the [value] row above
hactl auto create [target] = exempt: a create names nothing yet — the id comes out of the candidate, whose refusal is the [value] row above
hactl dash create [target] = exempt: a create names nothing yet — the url_path is a flag, judged on the [value] row above
hactl area create [target] = exempt: a create names nothing yet; the name it will mint is judged on the [value] row above
hactl floor create [target] = exempt: a create names nothing yet; the name it will mint is judged on the [value] row above
hactl label create [target] = exempt: a create names nothing yet; the name it will mint is judged on the [value] row above
hactl auto delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl script delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl tpl delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl helper delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl area delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl floor delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl label delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl config delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl dash delete [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl script run [value] = exempt: takes an identifier and nothing else — every caller-supplied value here IS the target
hactl auto rollback [value] = exempt: takes an optional identifier and nothing else; what is restored comes from the backup directory, not from the caller
hactl rollback [value] = exempt: same path as auto rollback and the same absence of a caller-supplied value

# --- debt: the rule applies and nothing proves it ----------------------------
hactl tpl create [target] = debt: a create names nothing yet, but the unique_id it mints must not collide, and nothing asserts what the preview does when it does
hactl tpl create [value] = debt: classifyTemplate hard-errors on unparseable YAML, a top-level list and an empty file before the plan (read 2026-07-26); a mapping with no recognised key still previews as an entity item and nothing asserts what --confirm does with it
hactl auto rollback [target] = debt: PlanRollback errors via findLatestBackup before the plan (read 2026-07-26); no test asserts it, and the raw "reading backup dir" message leaks when backups/ is absent
hactl rollback [target] = debt: same path as auto rollback and the same gap; no test asserts the refusal
hactl config flow-start [target] = debt: the dry run is proven to preview a domain that has a flow handler, but nothing asserts what it does with a domain that has none
hactl config flow-start [value] = debt: takes only the domain today; if it grows an initial-data flag the preview owes it the same judgement, and nothing would say so
hactl config flow-step [target] = debt: InspectFlow refuses an expired or never-started flow id before the plan (read 2026-07-26); no test asserts it
hactl config flow-step [value] = debt: --data is checked against the step's own schema fields, and nothing asserts what the preview does with a key the schema does not carry
hactl config options [target] = debt: resolveConfigEntry errors on an unknown entry and on one with no options flow, both before the plan (read 2026-07-26); no test asserts it
hactl config options [value] = debt: the options a caller sets are validated by HA on submit, and nothing asserts the preview refuses a value it will reject
hactl dash save [target] = debt: the JSON is validated and findDashboard resolves the url_path before the plan (read 2026-07-26), with a deliberate exception for the default empty path; no test asserts it
hactl dash save [value] = debt: --file is parsed before the plan; nothing asserts what the preview does with valid JSON that is not a Lovelace config
hactl dash replace [target] = debt: TestRunDashReplace_NotFound asserts the message for a value that is absent and exits zero; nothing asserts an unresolvable dashboard is refused
hactl dash replace [value] = debt: nothing asserts what the preview reports when <old> appears in no dashboard, or when <new> is malformed
hactl ent set-area [target] = debt: the area and the registry entry are both resolved before the plan (read 2026-07-26); no test asserts it
hactl ent set-area [value] = debt: the area name is the value HA judges, and the resolution above is the only thing standing in for that assertion
hactl ent set-label [target] = debt: every label and the entity are resolved before the plan (read 2026-07-26); no test asserts it
hactl ent set-label [value] = debt: the label names are the values HA judges, and the resolution above is the only thing standing in for that assertion
hactl ref replace [target] = debt: nothing asserts what the preview reports when the value to replace appears nowhere
hactl ref replace [value] = debt: nothing asserts what the preview does with a replacement that is not a valid entity id, which is the shape ent rename now refuses
hactl device set-area [value] = debt: the area is resolved by the same call the [target] row cites; nothing asserts a well-formed but unusable area value separately
hactl device set-label [value] = debt: the labels are resolved by the same call the [target] row cites; nothing asserts a well-formed but unusable label value separately
hactl script apply [value] = debt: TestE2ECreateDryRunValidatesInputCLI covers `script create`'s file; nothing asserts that `script apply` refuses a candidate the companion's dry-run write rejects
hactl companion wireguard config [value] = debt: --file is the tunnel config the add-on will install; nothing asserts the preview refuses a file it cannot parse
